  "seoBody": "<div class=\"key-takeaways\"><strong>Key takeaways</strong><ul><li>Compliance software and field service systems are different. Most small firms need only the capture part.</li><li>Certificate tools (iCertifi, Cert Lightning) do certificates well. They do not cover other inspections.</li><li>General inspection apps (iAuditor, GoAudits) cover any inspection but charge per seat.</li><li>Quickler is £75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts. No new app to install.</li><li>The right tool is the one people use on every job.</li></ul></div><h2>What \"getting compliant\" means</h2><p>It usually means one or more of these: make certificates for statutory inspections (EICR, CP12); keep inspection records for an audit (DVSA, HSE, local authority); show a client or insurer you took care; or win work that needs ISO 9001.</p><p>Work out which one applies. A sole electrician needs EICRs and CP12s, not a big property system. A gas contractor with landlord properties tracks certificate renewals. An H&amp;S consultancy makes site inspection and near-miss records.</p><h2>The four kinds of tool</h2><h3>Certificate tools</h3><p><strong>iCertifi</strong> and <strong>Cert Lightning</strong> are widely used for EICRs. They make the certificate in the right format. They do that one job well. They do not cover other inspections, like site checks, van checks or condition reports.</p><h3>General inspection apps</h3><p><strong>iAuditor (SafetyCulture)</strong> and <strong>GoAudits</strong> handle any inspection. You build the template, fill it on a phone and get a report. Both allow photos, offline use and PDF export. Both charge per seat, at £20 to £30 a seat a month. For ten or more people that adds up. iAuditor has more templates and analytics. GoAudits is often cheaper for small teams. Both need an app.</p><h3>WhatsApp-native tools</h3><p>Quickler sends the checklist to WhatsApp. You answer like any message, and send photos in the chat. No new app. No login.</p><p>It costs £75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts. Paid accounts have no limits: reports, photos and messages are unlimited. Start with a 14-day free trial. Everything is unlocked and you need no card to start.</p><p>Quickler fills in your own report layout. It handles any inspection, and works anywhere WhatsApp does. <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a>.</p><h3>Full field service systems</h3><p>ServiceTitan, Joblogic and Commusoft run the whole job: scheduling, dispatch, costing, invoicing and customers. Compliance is one part. They suit complex firms. For a small firm that needs compliance records, they are too much.</p><h2>The question that matters most: will your people use it?</h2><p>A common failure: a tool that shines in the demo. Three months later only two of eight people use it. The rest are back on paper, or fill it in from memory. The records are patchy.</p><p>Ask the adoption question first. Will people use it on every job without being chased?</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is the difference between compliance software and a field service system?</h3><p>Compliance software records inspections and makes the certificate or report. A field service system runs the whole job: scheduling, dispatch, invoicing and customers. Small firms often need only the first.</p><h3>Does an electrician need dedicated compliance software?</h3><p>Not always. Many use certificate tools such as Cert Lightning, iCertifi or ECA Site Assessment to make EICRs. You need more if you also run other inspections, track Faults across a portfolio, or report to clients.</p><h3>How much should a small firm pay?</h3><p>Certificate tools often cost £10 to £30 a month for each user. General inspection apps like iAuditor start at about £24 a seat a month. Quickler is £75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts. Start with a 14-day free trial. Everything is unlocked and you need no card to start.</p><h3>What matters most in compliance software?</h3><p>Whether people use it on site. A tool 40% of people use is worth less than a simpler one 95% use on every job.</p><h3>Compliance tools compared</h3><ul><li><strong>Certificate tools (iCertifi, Cert Lightning):</strong> best for EICR and CP12 work. £10 to £25 a month per user. App needed.</li><li><strong>Inspection apps (iAuditor, GoAudits):</strong> best for any inspection. £20 to £30 a seat a month. App needed.</li><li><strong>Quickler:</strong> any inspection, in WhatsApp. £75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts. No new app.</li><li><strong>Full field service (Joblogic, Commusoft):</strong> scheduling and compliance together. £40 to £80 a seat a month. Full set-up.</li></ul><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/field-reporting-software-uk.html\">Field reporting software for compliance workflows</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/inspection-software-uk-sme.html\">Inspection software for small teams</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/paperless-inspections-uk-trades.html\">Paperless inspections for UK trades</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a></li></ul>",
